PROBLEM STATEMENT:
Given a dataset (sales_data_sample.csv), perform data preprocessing, determine 
the optimal number of clusters using the Elbow Method (WCSS/Inertia), and apply 
both K-Means Clustering and Hierarchical (Agglomerative) Clustering. Compare 
and interpret the results.

CORE CONCEPTS:
- Unsupervised Learning: Finding hidden patterns or groupings in unlabeled data.
- K-Means Clustering: A centroid-based partitioning algorithm that divides data 
  into K non-overlapping subgroups by minimizing the Within-Cluster Sum of 
  Squares (WCSS / Inertia).
- Hierarchical Clustering: Creates a tree-like hierarchy of clusters 
  (Dendrogram) using a bottom-up (Agglomerative) or top-down (Divisive) approach.
